  "key_observation": "Price made a higher high near 15466.7 while RSI made a lower high after exiting the overbought zone (>70) and re-entering the 70/30 range, forming a regular bearish divergence that triggered the short entry.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a higher high in price near 15466.7 (visible on f004–f006) while RSI simultaneously formed a lower high (visible on f001/f007).",
    "Step 2: Applied the 'secret sauce' filter: confirmed RSI had exited the overbought zone (>70) and then re-entered the 70/30 range before the divergence signal was acted upon.",
    "Step 3: Entered a short position at the vertical line drawn where RSI re-entered the 70/30 range (as described at t=180.4s), with stop loss placed 50 points above entry.",
    "Step 4: Trailing take-profit by moving stop to break-even and shifting TP levels to successive swing lows as price declined, aiming for 1:4 risk-to-reward."
  ],
  "outcome": "Achieved approximately 1:4 R:R with a 50-point stop loss; profits trailed through successive swing lows until near maximum take-profit level.",
  "lessons": "Not all divergences are tradable—only the first divergence after RSI exits and re-enters the 70/30 range carries high probability; trailing stops lock in gains while letting winners run.",
